<content><![CDATA[
<p>The effective sharing and display of large data tables helped build the web as we know it. But tables are often difficult to manage on the web without understanding the complexities of HTML. Fortunately, HAX has built in support for editing tabular data.</p>
<h3 data-original-level="H3" id="header-d4c5e910-e607-24c8-26cb-c228f8a9e810">Example</h3>
<editable-table downloadable="" printable="" bordered="" condensed="" column-header="" row-header="" filter="" sort=""><table filter="">
	<thead class="thead">
		<tr class="thead-tr tr">
			<th scope="row" class="th th-or-td">Game Time</th>
			<th scope="col" class="th th-or-td">Location</th>
			<th scope="col" class="th th-or-td">Home</th>
			<th scope="col" class="th th-or-td">Away</th>
		</tr>
	</thead>
	<tbody class="tbody">
		<tr class="tbody-tr tr">
			<th scope="row" class="td th-or-td">4:00pm</th>
			<td class="td th-or-td">Local Pond</td>
			<td class="td th-or-td">Neighborhood kids</td>
			<td class="td th-or-td">Parents</td>
		</tr>
		<tr class="tbody-tr tr">
			<th scope="row" class="td th-or-td">5:00pm</th>
			<td class="td th-or-td">Local Pond</td>
			<td class="td th-or-td">Corner street</td>
			<td class="td th-or-td">Maple Street</td>
		</tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</editable-table>
